4. Phase Stability Index (PSI)
Definition

Phase Stability Index measures:

distance from fragmentation-sensitive transport phase boundaries.

PSI quantifies:

recursive stability,
spectral cohesion,
fragmentation proximity,
and transport regime organization.
Intuition

High PSI systems:

occupy stable robust transport regions,
preserve recursive continuity,
and resist perturbation collapse.

Low PSI systems:

approach fragmentation thresholds,
inflate recursive capacity,
and destabilize rapidly.
